 {
  "translated_term": "Umuntu ezindaba zabantu",
  "translation_rationale": "Digital Humanities ke umuntu apho uyaphila ukubona nokuthola kwa-bantu, nguwe ngumuntu ezindaba zabantu ngoba umuntu wakho uyaphila ukubona nokuthola kwenzulo zabantu kodwa bantu abo bazalwa nge-digital."
}

Explanation: The term "Digital Humanities" is translated as "Umuntu ezindaba zabantu". This translation is based on the fact that Digital Humanities involves studying and analyzing humanities (culture, arts, history, etc.) using digital tools and methods. In South Ndebele, "umuntu" means person or people, "ezindaba" means matters or issues, and "zabantu" is plural for people. So, "Umuntu ezindaba zabantu" can be interpreted as "matters of the people", which aligns with the concept of Digital Humanities.

