"Kernowek Digidhel" is the translation of "Digital Humanities". The term "digidhel" is derived from "digidhelia", which means digital in Cornish. The rationale behind this translation is that "Digital" in English refers to things related to computers or the internet, and "Kernowek Digidhel" means the study of these things as they relate to Cornish culture and language.

