Explanation:
The term "Digital Humanities" in Dinka is translated as "Dhiek-Nyang ma Thon-Thok ma Kuku-Kwot". The rationale behind this translation is that "Digital" (dhiek) refers to technology, "Humanities" (nyang) refers to the study of human culture and society, "ma" means "and", "thon-thok" means "technology" in a broader sense, and "kuku-kwot" means "study". Therefore, "Dhiek-Nyang ma Thon-Thok ma Kuku-Kwot" translates to "The study of human culture and society using technology and broader forms of technology."

